  "boundaries": [
    "Six real public-bootstrap histories use the native original-certificate overload after owner reopen; stable groups only. Actual local phases are reconstructed independently, never manufactured by recovery from witness hashes.",
    "Ten halt/SIGKILL cases use one separate three-voter EMPTY bootstrap/certificate prelude and twenty child JVMs. They do not establish power-loss or arbitrary concurrent network behavior.",
    "The initial source exposed a replay callback inventory-boundary error and an early test hook. That known-failed build was deliberately terminated after its eight application and three round-storage regressions passed. It is not successful full qualification.",
    "The final source passes thirteen selected Java tests. The earlier eleven tests are separately source-bound, not relabelled as executed on the final source.",
    "Normal, optimized and relocated original-first replay agree; complete interrupted/recovered files are checked. DATA image semantics use the existing Java typed-inspection assertions and byte binding; no new independent core serializer proof is claimed.",
    "Future target proof persistence, quorum selection propagation, actual dispatch, full offline-survivor continuation, automatic owner lifecycle and all remaining Phase 3 gates remain open.",
    "No public membership enablement, format/resource changes, protected CI, push, paid experiment or V5.2 runner changes."
  ],
